\section{Simplified Relationship Diagram}
The relationships can be read from the following text diagram:

\begin{lstlisting}[language={},numbers=none,xleftmargin=0pt,framexleftmargin=0pt,basicstyle=\footnotesize\ttfamily]
                 pygame.sprite.Sprite
                    /     |     \
                   /      |      \
                 Hero    Monster    Bullet

main.py creates and coordinates:
  Settings, Hero, Monster, Button, GameStats, HUD, Group

HUD ------ references ------> Settings
HUD ------ references ------> GameStats
HUD ------ references ------> Hero
Hero ----- references ------> Settings
Monster -- references ------> Settings
Bullet --- references ------> Settings (through constructor values)
GameStats - references -----> Settings
\end{lstlisting}

The arrows from the subclasses up to \code{Sprite} mean inheritance. The word \code{references} means that an object keeps a reference to another object or uses its data; it does not mean inheritance.

